WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.867
This morning.

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:01.634
Tokyo's Haneda

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.068
airport

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:05.405
expected to cancel more than 100 flights

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:05.972
after that

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.073
tragic collision

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.775
between a Japan Airlines

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:10.510
jet and a Japanese Coast Guard

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.644
plane on Tuesday,

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.513
killing five crew members on the Coast

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:14.414
Guard flight.

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.616
Also, newly released audio reveals

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.018
that air traffic control

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:20.153
had cleared the commercial flight to land

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:22.389
just before the two planes collided.

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:23.523
Joining us now is CNN's

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.759
Will Ripley live from Tokyo.

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:26.526
And Will,

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.762
what more have we learned of that audio

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:32.432
from air traffic control?

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:33.400
So we know

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.534
from the transport ministry

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.636
they've released the official transcript

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:37.470
of what happened

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.305
during those crucial 4 minutes

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:40.974
from 5:43 p.m.

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:43.076
local time to 5:47 p.m..

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:43.910
During those 4 minutes,

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.211
the Coast Guard

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.679
turboprop aircraft

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.815
was taxiing on the runway, one runway

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:49.883
getting ready to take off.

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:50.750
At the same time,

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.352
the Japan airliner

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:54.687
was making its final descent into Haneda.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.356
Listen now to the instructions

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:57.157
that were given.

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:58.224
First, you're going to hear

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.726
from the commercial flight

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:00.894
to air traffic control

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:01.294
and then you're going

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.062
to hear the instructions

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.563
that air traffic control gave

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:06.699
to that Coast Guard plane,

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:10.070
to a private company.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:13.006
Because this has been amazing

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:16.476
to have someone

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:17.811
every day with a number one,

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:22.649
I think a one of people.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.184
So that is the recording from the air

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.318
traffic control side.

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:25.618
You know,

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.253
the Japan airliner had the all clear

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.721
to land on runway C

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.156
and the Coast Guard plane

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.192
was told to proceed to the holding point,

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:33.660
basically stay in place

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.727
and stay there

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.096
until it's time for you to take off.

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:36.796
But, of course,

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.364
we know that the Coast Guard plane

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.432
was actually right

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.367
in the path of the Japan airliner

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:42.102
as it was landing

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:42.936
when the two planes hit.

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:44.737
There was that massive fireball.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:45.872
And of course, we know what happened.

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.373
Yet at least five of the Coast

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:49.008
Guard crew members were killed

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:50.477
and everybody on board

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:52.112
the plane was able to evacuate

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.313
with just seconds to spare.

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.881
But the crucial question,

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:56.783
did the Coast Guard pilot

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.318
not know where he was

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:58.818
or did air

00:01:58.818 --> 00:01:59.552
traffic control

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.321
not know the actual location of the plane

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.989
when they said to hold point?

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.791
And why did none of the three pilots

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.092
in the cockpit of the Japan

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.393
of the Japanese airliner

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.161
not see that

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:09.062
there was a plane

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.597
in the runway right in their path

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:12.098
and abort the landing?

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.666
They have not found the cockpit voice

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:14.934
recorder for the commercial plane.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:15.802
It's still sitting

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:16.903
right there in the middle of the runway,

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.671
a pile of metal and plastic.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:19.472
They have located

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.640
the cockpit voice recorder

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.841
for the Coast Guard aircraft.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:22.442
So those are going to be

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.643
the crucial questions

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.278
as they search for more answers

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.747
as to how all of this happened.

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.315
Well, Japan Airlines also said

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.584
the in-flight system malfunctioned.

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:32.085
I think what they said

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:33.520
during an evacuation of the passengers,

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.155
the crew was actually using a megaphone

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:35.788
to communicate.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:39.058
Well, what are we learning about this?

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:39.859
Yeah, we're getting

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:40.960
some really interesting

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.162
new video, eyewitness video

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:43.429
from inside the plane

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:45.098
during those crucial seconds.

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:46.199
And a lot of things

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:47.901
were actually going wrong.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:48.902
Some of the exit doors

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:50.436
passengers say were not operational.

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:51.171
And, yes, as you

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:52.038
mentioned,

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.940
the communication system of the plane

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:54.974
was not working,

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:56.109
which meant that the flight attendants

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.810
had to basically pull out the megaphones

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.380
and shout to get everybody off the plane.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:00.513
Well,

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:01.314
there was a lot of other

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:01.881
things happening.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:11.558
And take a look at this

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:21.401
from

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.736
what this video shows us is that, yes,

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:24.404
it was chaotic.

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:26.039
There was black smoke filling the cabin.

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:27.240
The flames were getting closer.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.042
They were just outside the windows.

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:29.642
People didn't

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.010
grab for their carry on bags.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:31.978
There was no arguing

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.213
or pushing and shouting.

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:35.148
People just listen to the instructions

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:37.183
and they got off the plane safely.

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:38.251
All of them did.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:39.452
It's a lesson for anyone

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:41.454
who travels and flies on planes

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:42.755
to look at very closely, guys.

